review_signals.comment:
![medium](https://www.gstatic.com/codereviewagent/medium-priority.svg)

The current implementation of `validate_grok1_expected_slots` has $O(N_{blocks} \times N_{slots} \times N_{tensors})$ complexity because it iterates over the entire tensor list for every block/slot combination. Since this is intended to be a strict validation pass, pre-grouping the tensors by their block and slot indices into a map would improve efficiency to $O(N_{tensors} \log N_{tensors})$ or $O(N_{tensors})$.

```rust
fn validate_grok1_expected_slots(inv: &ModelInventory, errors: &mut Vec<String>) {
    let mut by_slot: BTreeMap<(u32, u32), Vec<&TensorInfo>> = BTreeMap::new();
    for tensor in &inv.tensors {
        if let (Some(b), Some(s)) = (tensor.block_index, tensor.block_slot) {
            by_slot.entry((b, s)).or_default().push(tensor);
        }
    }

    for block_index in 0..GROK1_EXPECTED_BLOCKS {
        for slot in 0..12u32 {
            let tensors = by_slot.get(&(block_index, slot)).map(|v| v.as_slice()).unwrap_or(&[]);
            if tensors.is_empty() {
                errors.push(format!("missing block_{block_index:03}.slot_{slot:02}"));
            }
            if tensors.len() > 1 {
                errors.push(format!(
                    "duplicate block_{block_index:03}.slot_{slot:02} entries: {}",
                    tensors.len()
                ));
            }
            if let Some(tensor) = tensors.first() {
                validate_grok1_slot_tensor(tensor, errors);
            }
        }
    }
}
```

![medium](https://www.gstatic.com/codereviewagent/medium-priority.svg)

If `seen.len() != inv.tensors.len()` but `missing` is empty (which happens when `seen` contains extra/unrecognized tensors not present in `inv.tensors`), the error message will format with an empty `missing:` list. We can make the validation error clearer by explicitly handling the case where `missing` is empty. Additionally, ensure that regression tests are included to verify this specific validation failure case.

```rust
    if seen.len() != inv.tensors.len() {
        let missing = inv
            .tensors
            .iter()
            .filter(|tensor| !seen.contains_key(&(tensor.shard_ordinal, tensor.in_shard_index)))
            .map(tensor_identity_name)
            .collect::<Vec<_>>();
        if missing.is_empty() {
            bail!(
                "readiness groups cover {} tensors but inventory only has {}; there are extra/unrecognized tensors in the readiness report",
                seen.len(),
                inv.tensors.len()
            );
        } else {
            bail!(
                "readiness groups cover {} tensors but inventory has {}; missing: {}",
                seen.len(),
                inv.tensors.len(),
                missing.join(", ")
            );
        }
    }
```

<details>
<summary>References</summary>

1. When implementing strict validation for model manifests, include regression tests that verify specific failure cases, such as incorrect tensor kinds or shapes, to ensure the validation is not too permissive.
</details>

