![medium](https://www.gstatic.com/codereviewagent/medium-priority.svg)

Formatting the `QuantPolicy` enum to a `String` for every single tensor (which can be hundreds or thousands of tensors) in the loop introduces unnecessary string allocations and formatting overhead. Since `QuantPolicy` has a fixed set of variants, we can map them to `&'static str` using a match statement, and use `BTreeMap<&'static str, usize>` to avoid all allocations.

```suggestion
    let mut policy_counts: BTreeMap<&'static str, usize> = BTreeMap::new();
    for tensor in &manifest.tensors {
        let policy_name = match tensor.quant_policy {
            crate::schema::QuantPolicy::PassthroughF32Router => "PassthroughF32Router",
            crate::schema::QuantPolicy::PassthroughF32Norm => "PassthroughF32Norm",
            crate::schema::QuantPolicy::CandidateSaaqEmbedding => "CandidateSaaqEmbedding",
            crate::schema::QuantPolicy::WrapExistingInt8Expert => "WrapExistingInt8Expert",
            crate::schema::QuantPolicy::WrapExistingInt8Unknown => "WrapExistingInt8Unknown",
            crate::schema::QuantPolicy::UnknownPassthroughOrWarn => "UnknownPassthroughOrWarn",
        };
        *policy_counts.entry(policy_name).or_insert(0) += 1;
    }
```

